INNER JOIN vs LEFT JOIN
INNER JOIN	LEFT JOIN
Only matching rows	All rows from the left table
Removes unmatched rows	Keeps unmatched rows from the left table
Most commonly used	Useful when you want every record from the left table
LEFT JOIN vs RIGHT JOIN
LEFT JOIN	RIGHT JOIN
Keeps left table	Keeps right table
Most commonly used	Used less frequently
Common Interview Questions
Q1. What is the difference between INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN?

Answer:

INNER JOIN returns only matching records.
LEFT JOIN returns all rows from the left table plus matching rows from the right table. Unmatched right-side values become NULL.

Q2. Which JOIN returns all rows from both tables?
Answer: FULL OUTER JOIN.

Q3. Which JOIN creates a Cartesian Product?
Answer: CROSS JOIN.

Q4. Why do we use aliases (AS)?
To make queries shorter, cleaner, and easier to read.

Example:

SELECT e.Name, d.Department
FROM Employees e
JOIN Departments d
ON e.Dept_ID = d.Dept_ID;

Q5. What is a Cartesian Product?
Every row of the first table combines with every row of the second table.

Example:
3 rows × 5 rows = 15 rows.

Memory Trick

INNER JOIN  → Only Match
LEFT JOIN   → Keep Left
RIGHT JOIN  → Keep Right
FULL JOIN   → Keep Both
CROSS JOIN  → Everything × Everything
SELF JOIN   → Table joins itself
